-- #1002 fixture, module 4 of 4 — the ORDINARY IMPL SPELLING.
--
-- Note the import list: `iface.{Sized, Box, Small}` — the INTERFACE, not the
-- method. Writing an impl never requires importing the method name, and this is
-- the spelling most real code uses.
--
-- This is the F2 regression the #1007 review caught: keying an impl head by the
-- bare method name through `useEnv` MISSED here (nothing bound `sizeOf` locally),
-- so the head fell through to `?ext|method|sizeOf` — every impl written this way
-- collapsing onto one key, detached from its interface. `main.mdk` only avoided
-- it by also CALLING the method and therefore having to import the name.
--
-- The head below must land on `iface|method|sizeOf`, same as every other impl of
-- `Sized`, with no method import anywhere in this file.
import iface.{Sized, Box, Small}

data Sack =
  | Sack

impl Sized Sack where
  sizeOf Sack = 3

export aBox : Box
aBox = Small
